<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Deskify is intentionally NOT App-Sandboxed. Its core job — reading,
      moving, and closing OTHER applications' windows via the Accessibility
      API, and launching arbitrary apps the user chose — is fundamentally
      incompatible with the sandbox, which confines an app to its own
      container. This is the same reason window-manager utilities on macOS
      ship un-sandboxed (and therefore outside the Mac App Store).

      Accessibility control itself needs NO entitlement — it is granted by the
      user at runtime through TCC (System Settings → Privacy & Security →
      Accessibility). The entries below only matter under the Hardened Runtime
      (which notarization requires):
    -->

    <!-- Allows sending Apple Events, which NSWorkspace app activation can use. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
